                 ⚠ SCOPE of road_grid_levels_pkg, narrower than upstream. Depths
                 are whole half-steps so the half-step offset is exact; upstream
                 uses REAL arithmetic and DY = max(0.01, ZONES(NZONE)/n). Only
                 the FLAT grid is modelled — the exponential grid of the ELSE
                 branch (lines 178-206) is not, nor the material-property
                 interpolation that follows (lines 210-240). Upstream bounds
                 ir40 by iref as well; this core characterises each count on
                 its own. Upstream never initialises ir40 when no level lies at
                 or above the sensor; this core returns 0 there, which is a
                 choice, not a re-expression. Levels are capped at 200 and the
                 half-step at 1000 units. Flux_Depth and Temperature_Depth are
                 definitions with no contract.

                 WHAT IS PROVED: the level count within the structure depth is
                 exactly the largest level whose flux depth does not exceed it
                 (its own depth fits, the next does not); the count at or above
                 the sensor is exactly the largest level whose temperature depth
                 does not exceed it, or zero. Both are facts about integer
                 division against the two depth formulas.

